  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Labor Mobility Pathways for Persons with Humanitarian Needs in Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNHCR and IOM pilot project seeks to pave the way towards an alternative migration regularization process for those vulnerable migrants of Haitian origin who would not be recognized as refugees but cannot be returned to their countries of origin and want to stay in Mexico. It is aimed that in this first phase 50 households, with family members of working-age from 18 to 65 years old &#x2013;identified in Tapachula and Ciudad Acu&#xf1;a-, will be supported on their regularization processes and their socio-economic integration in the Municipalities of Puebla and San Luis Potosi in collaboration with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the National Migration Institute.</narrative>
  </description>
